# ${project.name}

This is a collection of templates that are specific to the Maven project. They are probably not of interest to projects other than Apache Maven.

Below you will find a listing of the resources that can be found in the current version (${project.version}) of Maven Shared Resources. They are listed by which plugin they are meant to be used with.

Maven Checkstyle Plugin
-----------------------

#[[### `config/maven-header.txt`]]#

This is a license header template that can be used by Maven Checkstyle Plugin to verify that all files are using this license header.

#[[### [`config/maven_checks.xml`](./maven_checks.html)]]#

This is a Checkstyle configuration file for [Maven coding conventions](/developers/conventions/code.html) that can be used in Maven Checkstyle Plugin.

#[[### `config/maven_checks_nocodestyle.xml`]]#

The same Checkstyle rules without the layout, import and header checks that Spotless covers. The Maven parent POM uses this one.

Spotless Maven Plugin
---------------------

#[[### `config/maven-header-plain.txt`]]#

The license header as plain text, for the Spotless `licenseHeader` step.

#[[### `config/maven-eclipse-importorder.txt`]]#

The import order, for the Spotless `importOrder` step. Eclipse can import it too.

#[[### `config/maven-groovy-eclipse.properties`]]#

Groovy-Eclipse formatter settings for Groovy scripts, such as invoker hook scripts, for the Spotless `greclipse` step.

Eclipse code formatter
----------------------

#[[### `config/maven-eclipse-codestyle.xml`]]#

An Eclipse formatter profile matching palantir-java-format, which can be imported into the IDE.

IntelliJ IDEA code formater
---------------------------

#[[### `config/maven-idea-codestyle-2022.xml`]]#

This is IntelliJ IDEA code formater which can be imported into IDE. It approximates palantir-java-format for Java; to get the exact output, install the palantir-java-format IntelliJ plugin.

Usage
-----

General instructions on how to use the Maven Shared Resources can be found on the [usage page](./usage.html).
